#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bb-login <site> [--user U] [--url URL] [--keep] [--notify] [--json] [--force] [--wait N]

Hands-free login for the browser agent: the agent is the owner's hands.
One hidden broker lease (windowless Brave when the machine has it, else a hidden tab in his
Brave; never bb-show), opens the site's login page from the password vault entry (reached over ssh, see login.env), fills username +
password, submits, and reports one of:

  logged_in | already_logged_in | captcha | wrong_password | needs_code | stuck | no_vault_entry | refused

2FA: when a code is asked it polls for a FRESH code (arrived after this login started) in
the owner's texts (Messages chat.db, read-only) and email through a mail API, types it and submits.
No code in --wait seconds (default 90): texts the owner one line ("text me the code") and keeps
watching 2 more minutes, so a code texted back from his phone is used too.

Captcha: returns status captcha with a crop path and keeps the tab (owner printed) so the
calling chat can solve it with ~/Scripts/bb-captcha. No second captcha solver here.

Never prints a password or a code. One tab, one lease, no reloads; the tab is closed at the
end unless --keep (or a captcha) keeps it; a kept tab closes itself when the lease runs out
(KEEP_TTL) or with `BROKER_URL=<broker> bb-close <owner>`.

Exit: 0 logged in (or already) · 2 needs code · 3 captcha · 4 wrong password · 5 stuck
      6 no vault entry · 7 refused (bank/gov/one-session site without --force)

Config: environment variables, or ~/.config/browser-agent/login.env (KEY=value lines, git-ignored,
never in the repo). Keys:
  BA_PHONE          owner's phone number digits (to spot a code the owner texts back; notify target)
  BA_ECHO           the chat identifier your own outbound texts echo into (skipped when reading codes)
  BA_SEND           script that sends a text: called as `script "message"`
  BA_VAULT_SSH      ssh host alias that holds the vault
  BA_VAULT_FILE     path on that host to the vault passwords.json (list of {site,url,user,password})
  BA_CHATDB_SSH     optional ssh command words used to read chat.db when this process lacks Full Disk Access
  BA_MAIL_ENV       colon-separated env files holding a mail API url and token (key names: BA_MAIL_URL_KEY / BA_MAIL_TOKEN_KEY, default MAIL_API_URL / MAIL_API_TOKEN)
  BA_MAIL_ACCOUNTS  comma-separated account names for the mail API
  BA_LOGIN_URLS     optional json file mapping a vault host to its real login url
  BA_HIDDEN_PROFILE optional dir of a windowless browser profile; when present, logins run there
  BA_NEVER_RE       optional extra regex of hosts to refuse
"""
